{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the hosted agent's run and head 469306a3, for request 7ba98c19 and review request f0b7b5ad. Verdict: APPROVED. This head may land. A script drove one hosted agent to a proposal on the deployed dap-demo Worker, the evidence holds what the note says, and each done-when item is met for a scripted run. No claim about a model rests on it.\n\n## The run, from the public lines\n\nI read each of the 29 phases' lines in `run/lines/`, not the note's summary.\n\n- **The loop.** All 29 exited 0, and the transcript holds one row per phase. The issue lane's facts run in order at seqs 2 to 12, and each step's fact is on its line. `agent-verify` reads the two orders back, with 19 entries.\n- **The proposal.** `agent-propose` is seq 4 at `sc_efkizv2e…`, hash `38fdd405…`, and `agent-verify` prints the same fact. Base and head are both `f07f4647…`, with `baseIsHead` true and `standIn` false.\n- **The wait.** `agent-wait` started at 00:39:38, before `approve` at 00:39:46 and `decide` at 00:39:50, and it ran 16.55 s in one round. Its fact is the person's `decide`: seq 8, hash `ac0af659…`.\n- **The resume.** `agent-resume` is a new session, and it prints the same decision fact and the terms at seq 9.\n- **The sessions.** 14 agent lines print 14 different session digests.\n- **The tools.** The list holds the 11 generic names, and the list has 57 tools until the change lane opens. The digest moves once, from `ecba05c0…` to `a943e842…`, at `agent-link`. The later list has 71 tools, with the same 11 generic names and the same prompt digest. `issue.approve`, `issue.decide` and `change.merge` appear on neither list. The file comparison in `run/hosted-tools-compare.txt` exits 0.\n\n## Your list\n\n- **Item 1, one version on all 29: enough.** A line that printed the version would add little, because each phase compares it with `/health` before it does anything. T1 and T2 hold that check, `/health` answered it before and after, and the planner's receipts show no other deployment on dap-demo until 01:00.\n- **Item 7, the scan: the slip costs little, and you reported it plainly.** I scanned `lines`, `diagnostics` and `after` myself: 122 files. I found no link prefix, no `Bearer ` or `Control ` header, no private key name, no bearer shape and no `TEST ` text. Every long token is a scope, incarnation, key or digest shape, or the version UUID. I hold no exact link value, so this shows shapes only, and the exact link rests on each line's own scan, as you say.\n- **Item 9.** The input's home no longer exists on this machine. `POST /mcp` on dap-demo answered 404 at 01:10.\n\n## Your three questions\n\n1. **Yes, the done-when depends on the script's structure in two ways that the note does not state. Neither blocks.** First, the operator's command chooses each next phase. So \"a fresh session resumes from the record alone\" means that a new session can rebuild the block, the decision and the offer. It does not mean that a session can tell from the record what to do next. Second, `Room.lane` requires exactly one issue lane and one change lane, and `rebuild` requires one blocked block, so the run shows this in a scratch room with one of each. A room with several would stop the script. Add both to \"What the run's words mean\" at the next edit of that note. Any report of this run should keep to them.\n2. **The request is still met.** Its done-when asks for the loop, the tools and a fresh session, and it does not ask for recovery on the Worker. The note lists what did not run live, and the scripted tests cover those answers.\n3. **The `invite-agent` recheck: remove it in a later head, at the next change to this script.** It does no harm. It is one more loop that the engine now makes unnecessary.\n\n## What the run does not show\n\n- A model following the prompt or choosing among the tools.\n- That the host holds `f07f4647…`. The record held that head and the proposal signed it.\n- Any recovery path on the Worker, because no phase stopped.\n- A merge. The proposal stays open, and no phase asks for one.\n- The act tools' shape as a hosted default, beyond the form check and the person-only list.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n**Architecture.** Sound. The head adds an example script, its tests and its note. Against main, it changes two lines of `identities.ts`' owner check, one type in `diagnostics.ts`, and `tsconfig.json`. No hosted code changes.\n\n**Security.** No blocking issue. The endpoint stayed open from 00:31 to 01:00 by the planner's decision, and it is closed. The bearer stays valid on the Worker with no copy held, so it can only matter if someone recovered that deleted home. The scratch room and its agent stay on dap-demo.\n\n**Simplification.** Acceptable. Later work can remove the recheck.\n\n## What I checked\n\n- **Script.** `git diff bed1c8be 469306a3 -- examples/repo-in-ai/hosted-loop` is empty.\n- **Evidence.** `SHA256SUMS` hashes to `8bfd355c…`, each listed file verifies, and no file is writable. `run/SHA256SUMS` hashes to `1080e268…`, and each of its files verifies. `run/head.txt` names bed1c8be. `run/target.txt` names version `de8427ec`, commit de53d89a and receipt `2894b43a`.\n- **Gate and controls.** I read these as recorded and did not rerun them: the gate at `f6c6ef9c`, the 43 controls and the local run. The note states their digests, and the head after that checkpoint adds only the note and its manifest.\n- **Tests I ran at this head.** `hosted-loop.test.ts` passes 204 of 204, and `hosted-loop.scope.test.ts` passes 1 of 1. `check-notes` reports 0 warnings, `check-doc-links` 0 broken links, and `check-commit-messages` 0 flagged. The worktree stayed clean. The head includes main fd69c867.\n- **Not done.** I used no independent reader. I could not read the scratch room on the Worker, because no key to it remains, so I hold only the public lines and did not recompute the entries' hashes. I did not read `hl-run.py` or `scan.py` beyond their results.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5